{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Hit Theaters with a $50 Million Budget\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction novel, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of approximately $104.5 million.\n\nThe film, which debuted in the top spot at the box office in its opening weekend, earned $21,103,203 during that initial North American release. In the United States, it remained in the top ten for its first four weeks. The total domestic gross reached over $51 million, with international markets contributing an additional $53.4 million to its global total.",
